/// known-gap: interp has no concurrency builtins (VM only, spec 2026-10-08)
/// An actor runs handler(state, message) for each message in order; the handler's result is the next state. :await on a request gives the state right after that message; :await on the actor, after :halt, gives its final state.
act count(state, msg)
    :update!(state{"n"}, state{"n"} + msg)
    return state
xx
box | {"n": 0}
h | :actor(box, count)
say(:valtype(h))
say(:post(h, 5))
:post(h, 7)
say(:await(:request(h, 1)){"n"})
:post(h, 100)
:halt(h)
say(:await(h){"n"})
